The published packages and container images embed or depend on third-party
work under its own terms:

- ONNX Runtime (MIT). Bundled by the `postvec-onnxruntime` package and the
  complete container image; its license text ships with the bundle.
- sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (Apache License 2.0). The default
  model bundled by the `postvec-model-*` package and the complete image; its
  LICENSE travels inside the model archive, and the Debian package renders it
  into /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright
  (packaging/postvec/model/copyright.in).
- pgvector (PostgreSQL License). A runtime dependency of the extension,
  installed from its own packages; not bundled here.
- memberlist (MPL-2.0). The gossip implementation `postvec-server` uses for
  cluster membership. Linked unmodified; the MPL's obligations attach to that
  crate's own files, not to this repository's.
- The Rust dependency tree, under the licenses its crates declare
  (`cargo license` in this repository enumerates them). The release pipeline's
  audit gate (packaging/postvec/scripts/audit.sh) runs against both lockfiles.

The `engine/` and `shared/` crates are a trimmed fork of UniVec's internal
inference engine; see engine/FORK.md for provenance and the deletion record.

Some identifiers predate this repository and are kept for wire and tooling
compatibility rather than renamed: "ravenna" (the `x-ravenna-error-code`
gRPC metadata header, a live wire contract), "aphex" (the model registry's
publication tooling, visible in registry index metadata), and "nin"/
"ninference" (the inference engine and its protocol, as in
`proto/ninference.proto`). They are internal project names, not third-party
trademarks.
